{
  "description": "Openable URL vectors (isUrl). Spec: docs/protocol.md, \"Text messages\", \"Links\". For every case: isOpenableUrl(text) must equal isUrl. The rule applies to the trimmed text; a sender sets isUrl to this value, and a receiver offers Open only if isUrl is true and the rule holds for the text it received. Strings use \\u escapes for every non-ASCII character.",
  "specVersion": 1,
  "howToRead": "input is the text as the sender holds it (it may carry leading and trailing whitespace). A case with synthesize has no input: the text is prefix + fill repeated fillCount times + suffix, and the trimmed text is trimmedBytes bytes of UTF-8. Whitespace is the Unicode White_Space set listed in the spec (U+0009 to U+000D, U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000 to U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000), which is not what every platform's isWhitespace() means: implement the list. Control characters are U+0000 to U+001F and U+007F to U+009F. Do not use a URL library for this rule. Since changelog 55 an authority with @, a backslash or a percent sign is not openable, and neither is a host with [ ] < > ^ | (outside an IPv6 literal).",
  "maxBytes": 8192,
